{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Behold, their Arielim.</b> Some say it is derived from Ariel, as if he said 'their Ariel,' and it is not correct in the sense of the pericope. Some say they are two words, 'I will see them'; this too is far-fetched. The correct view in my eyes is that the word Arielim is like 'their messengers,' and the proof is 'messengers of peace' (Isaiah 33:7), and like it 'the two Ariel of Moab' (2 Samuel 23:20). The sense is that the messengers of every nation who seek peace in the world will weep when the kingdom of Assyria rules."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:28.303978585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}